// One NV40 fragment instruction carries ONE inline constant block, and a
// comparison of a uniform against a literal has two constant operands.
// The general path appended a 16-byte block for each, after the same
// instruction: the second block was then decoded as an instruction (the
// disassembler reads it as NOPR), so the ucode was not merely wrong, it
// was malformed - and the comparison's second operand resolved to the
// first block, making `u_t > 0.0` into `u_t > u_t` (t_40dd8159).
//
// needsInlineConstPreload in legalizeInputOperands has always handled this
// shape; comparisons were absent from the list of ops that pass looks at,
// so they never reached it.  The reference preloads the uniform into a
// register and keeps the literal inline.
//
// The assertion is that no instruction carries more than one const block,
// which the ucode walk can check exactly: a block follows the instruction
// that names it.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, uniform float u_t, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    float t = (u_t > 0.0) ? 1.0 : 0.0;
    o = float4(t, c.y, c.z, 1.0);
}
